127	    /* ---------------------------
128	     |  Keep model-returning helpers (no model caching)
129	     * --------------------------*/
130	
131	    /**
132	     * Resolve a Professional by their Supabase auth UUID.
133	     *
134	     * auth_user_id is immutable — set at account creation, never updated — so there is
135	     * no real mid-request race between the cached ID lookup and the model fetch.
136	     * The mismatch guard below is a belt-and-suspenders defence against stale/corrupt
137	     * cache entries only, not a concurrency fix.
138	     *
139	     * Two-level cache:
140	     *   1. id lookup (`pro:map:auth:{uid}`) — 30 min, immutable mapping
141	     *   2. hydrated model (`pro:model:{id}`) — 60 s with SWR + jitter via CacheLockService
142	     *
143	     * The model layer is what makes the auth path a Redis hit instead of a Postgres
144	     * round-trip on every authenticated request. Eloquent models serialize cleanly
145	     * through Redis; relations preserved across the boundary stay marked as loaded
146	     * (so `$pro->site` does not silently re-query). Bust both keys on profile writes
147	     * via `invalidateProfessional()`.
